{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Field.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Field.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"field field","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Field.md","fileName":"Field.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Field","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ring and Ideal Foundations]] · [[Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic","Commutative Ring","Multiplicative Inverse","Integral Domain","Maximal Ideal","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Field.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Field.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"field field","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Field.md","fileName":"Field.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Field","heading":"Field","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A field is a nonzero [[Commutative Ring]] in which every nonzero element has a [[Multiplicative Inverse]]. Its only ideals are the zero ideal and the whole ring.\n\nEvery field is an [[Integral Domain]]. Conversely, a quotient by a [[Maximal Ideal]] is a field, so maximal ideals mark the places where a ring can be reduced to field-valued arithmetic.\n\nThe book moves from fields as special domains to fields as coefficient systems for polynomial division and as the base and extension objects of Galois theory. Finite domains and maximal-ideal quotients provide two important constructions of fields.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ring and Ideal Foundations","Integral Domains and Ring Characteristic","Commutative Ring","Multiplicative Inverse","Integral Domain","Maximal Ideal","commutativealgebra.pdf","essentialsofmodernalgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pa